<LanguageData>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.SharedSettingsTabLabel>Shared</ColonyManagerRedux.SharedSettingsTabLabel>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.JobDefaultsTabLabel>Job Defaults</ColonyManagerRedux.JobDefaultsTabLabel>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.GeneralSettingsTabLabel>General</ColonyManagerRedux.GeneralSettingsTabLabel>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.DoVerboseLogging>DEV: Enable verbose logging</ColonyManagerRedux.DoVerboseLogging>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.DoVerboseLogging.Tip>Enables verbose logging for the mod. This will log a lot of information to the log file, which can be useful for debugging issues, but will write a lot to the log relatively quickly. Use only when necessary.</ColonyManagerRedux.DoVerboseLogging.Tip>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.ManagerDefaultUpdateInterval>Default update interval</ColonyManagerRedux.ManagerDefaultUpdateInterval>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.NewJobsAreImmediatelyOutdated>New jobs should be immediately handled</ColonyManagerRedux.NewJobsAreImmediatelyOutdated>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.NewJobsAreImmediatelyOutdated.Tip>When this setting is enabled, a newly created manager job will immediately require a manager to go deal with it. Otherwise, the job will start out as updated and not be worked on until its update interval elapses for the first time.</ColonyManagerRedux.NewJobsAreImmediatelyOutdated.Tip>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.RecordHistoricalData>Record historical data</ColonyManagerRedux.RecordHistoricalData>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.RecordHistoricalData.Tip>With this setting enabled, the mod will, for each manager job that exists, ask it to record its data a certain number of times per day, data which later gets used to show graphs of how the values have changed over time. This data recording process isn't free, so if you're having performance issues, you could try turning this setting off.</ColonyManagerRedux.RecordHistoricalData.Tip>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.NewJobsShouldBeResourceLocked>New jobs should be resource locked</ColonyManagerRedux.NewJobsShouldBeResourceLocked>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.NewJobsShouldBeResourceLocked.Tip>When this setting is enabled, new jobs that let you select which map resources to gather start out locked to only allow you from choosing the resources that map can possibly provide. Otherwise, new jobs will start out letting you pick from all the resources registered with the game, even those not normally possible on the map.</ColonyManagerRedux.NewJobsShouldBeResourceLocked.Tip>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.ManagerSettings.NoMaxDesignationsPerJob>Jobs can manage as many designations as they need to meet targets</ColonyManagerRedux.ManagerSettings.NoMaxDesignationsPerJob>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.ManagerSettings.MaxDesignationsPerJob>Jobs can only manage up to {0} designations at any time</ColonyManagerRedux.ManagerSettings.MaxDesignationsPerJob>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.ManagerSettings.MaxDesignationsPerJob.Tip>A manager will only maintain as many designations as this setting allows for, even if it's fewer than it would take to meet a job target. Note that not necessarily all types of manager jobs can or will respect this setting.</ColonyManagerRedux.ManagerSettings.MaxDesignationsPerJob.Tip>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.ShowInfoCardButtonsWherePossible>Show info card buttons where possible</ColonyManagerRedux.ShowInfoCardButtonsWherePossible>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.ShowInfoCardButtonsWherePossible.Tip>When this setting is enabled, info card buttons will be shown for things in manager jobs where applicable, providing quick access to relevant information.</ColonyManagerRedux.ShowInfoCardButtonsWherePossible.Tip>
