    <ColonyManagerRedux.PerformanceSettingsTabLabel>Performance</ColonyManagerRedux.PerformanceSettingsTabLabel>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.PerformanceSettings.OperationsPerTick>Operations per tick: {0}</ColonyManagerRedux.PerformanceSettings.OperationsPerTick>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.PerformanceSettings.OperationsPerTick.Tip>Controls how many operations can be performed per game tick. What exactly counts as an operation is decided on a case-by-case basis. Lower values may help improve performance but also increases the time it takes for jobs to complete. Very low values can make jobs take extremely long to complete.</ColonyManagerRedux.PerformanceSettings.OperationsPerTick.Tip>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.PerformanceSettings.TicksBetweenOperations>Ticks between operations: {0}</ColonyManagerRedux.PerformanceSettings.TicksBetweenOperations>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.PerformanceSettings.TicksBetweenOperations.Tip>Controls how many ticks must pass between doing operations. Higher values may help improve performance but also increases the time it takes for jobs to complete. Very high values can make jobs take extremely long to complete.</ColonyManagerRedux.PerformanceSettings.TicksBetweenOperations.Tip>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.PerformanceSettings.AdvancedPerformanceSettings>Advanced: Enable per-operation performance settings</ColonyManagerRedux.PerformanceSettings.AdvancedPerformanceSettings>
    <ColonyManagerRedux.PerformanceSettings.AdvancedPerformanceSettings.Tip>This allows you to configure performance options on a per-operation basis instead of using a single value globally for fine tuning.</ColonyManagerRedux.PerformanceSettings.AdvancedPerformanceSettings.Tip>
